1 0 0 1 54 790 Tm (" Provide a structured and fair mechanism to assess student skills.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 776 Tm (" Compute readiness against internship templates using configured skill requirements.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 762 Tm (" Support mentorship request, review, roadmap, and validation workflows.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 748 Tm (" Enforce clean separation of concerns through a 3-tier facade-driven architecture.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 734 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 720 Tm (1.5 Problem Statement) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 706 Tm (Students require an integrated system that can quantify current skill proficiency, identify) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 692 Tm (readiness gaps for target internship domains, and connect mentorship actions to measurable) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 678 Tm (progression. MICHIRU addresses this by combining assessment, readiness analytics, and) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 664 Tm (mentorship operations in one coherent platform.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 650 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 636 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 622 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 608 Tm (2. Overall Description) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 594 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 580 Tm (2.1 Product Perspective) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 566 Tm (MICHIRU is a JavaFX desktop application backed by MySQL. The implementation follows a strict) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 552 Tm (3-tier structure:) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 538 Tm (" View layer \(*ViewController classes\) for interaction and rendering.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 524 Tm (" Facade layer \(AccessAndOverviewFacade, CatalogAndInternshipFacade, EvaluationFacade,) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 510 Tm (MentorshipLifecycleFacade\) for use-case orchestration.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 496 Tm (" Database handler layer \(MySQLHandler\) for persistence through JDBC.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 482 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 468 Tm (2.2 Product Functions) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 454 Tm (" User registration and login with role-based dashboard routing.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 440 Tm (" Skill catalog, question bank, and internship template management.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 426 Tm (" Skill assessment attempt flow with scoring and proficiency updates.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 412 Tm (" Readiness computation against internship templates.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 398 Tm (" Mentorship request, approval/decline, roadmap and progress workflows.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 384 Tm (" Validation request submission and review cycle.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 370 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 356 Tm (2.3 List of Use Cases) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 342 Tm (" UC01 Register) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 328 Tm (" UC02 Submit Skill Validation Request) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 314 Tm (" UC03 Manage Skill Catalog) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 300 Tm (" UC04 Manage Internships) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 286 Tm (" UC05 Configure Question Bank) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 272 Tm (" UC06 Take Skill Assessment) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 258 Tm (" UC07 Assess Readiness) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 244 Tm (" UC08 Request Mentorship) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 230 Tm (" UC09 Review Mentorship Requests) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 216 Tm (" UC10 Generate Roadmap) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 202 Tm (" UC11 Validate Skill Proficiency) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 188 Tm (" UC12 Track Mentorship Progress) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 174 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 160 Tm (2.4 Extended Use Cases) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 146 Tm (Extended behavior is defined in the fully dressed use case set through alternative and) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 132 Tm (exception scenarios, including insufficient data conditions, cancellation flows, and) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 118 Tm (validation constraints.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 104 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 90 Tm (2.5 Use Case Diagram) Tj
