1 0 0 1 54 748 Tm (3. Other Nonfunctional Requirements) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 734 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 720 Tm (3.1 Performance Requirements) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 706 Tm (" UI interactions should remain responsive with practical target response under one second for) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 692 Tm (standard local operations.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 678 Tm (" Business processing is centralized in facades to reduce repeated UI-side computation.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 664 Tm (" Data retrieval uses bounded queries and operation-specific access methods for predictable) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 650 Tm (runtime behavior.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 636 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 622 Tm (3.2 Safety Requirements) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 608 Tm (" Assessment and mentorship operations maintain controlled state transitions to avoid invalid) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 594 Tm (updates.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 580 Tm (" Submission and review paths are guarded by role context and active relationship checks.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 566 Tm (" Error handling paths return users to stable states without corrupting persisted domain) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 552 Tm (records.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 538 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 524 Tm (3.3 Security Requirements) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 510 Tm (" JDBC operations rely on parameterized execution patterns consistent with PreparedStatement) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 496 Tm (usage to reduce SQL injection exposure.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 482 Tm (" Authentication context is enforced before role-scoped actions are executed.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 468 Tm (" Sensitive operations \(proficiency updates, readiness records, mentorship transitions\) are) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 454 Tm (performed through controlled facade entry points rather than UI-level direct access.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 440 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 426 Tm (3.4 Software Quality Attributes) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 412 Tm (" Maintainability: clear 3-tier decomposition with facade boundaries.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 398 Tm (" Modifiability: business rules isolated from UI controllers and persistence details.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 384 Tm (" Testability: facade-level use-case methods provide stable orchestration units.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 370 Tm (" Consistency: common flow control and validation standards across controllers.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 356 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 342 Tm (3.5 Business Rules) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 328 Tm (" Role-driven capabilities are enforced for Student, Mentor, and Internship Coordinator.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 314 Tm (" Assessment outcomes determine proficiency progression according to configured thresholds.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 300 Tm (" Readiness is evaluated against internship template skill requirements and weights.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 286 Tm (" Mentorship and validation workflows require active contextual constraints before state) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 272 Tm (updates.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 258 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 244 Tm (3.6 Operating Environment) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 230 Tm (" Java Runtime: Java 17.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 216 Tm (" Application Framework: JavaFX.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 202 Tm (" Database: MySQL \(InnoDB\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 188 Tm (" Data Access: JDBC.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 174 Tm (" Desktop execution environment for end users.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 160 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 146 Tm (3.7 User Interfaces) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 132 Tm (The system uses JavaFX scene-based interfaces with dedicated controller classes for each) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 118 Tm (functional module. UI behavior includes role dashboards, form-based CRUD operations, guided) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 104 Tm (assessment modal flows, and progress-oriented panels for mentorship and readiness review. The) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 90 Tm (user interface layer is intentionally restricted to interaction handling, presentation state,) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 76 Tm (and navigation, while business orchestration and persistence remain outside the UI tier.) Tj
ET
endstream
